{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/833621-kith-permutations-changing-the-flavor","id":833621,"title":"Kith permutations: Changing the flavor","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-19T18:11:31-08:00","id":833621,"title":"Kith permutations: Changing the flavor","content":"I thought it might be fun to examine new potential flavors for the Kiths, maintaining the same mechanics. <br /> <br /> For example:<br /> <br /> Verminswarm (Sandharrowed):Transformed into a hive of bees, a nest of ants, or some other collection of insects, the Changeling had to pull himself together in a more literal fashion than most in order to escape. Perhaps he exists simply as a man-shaped bundle of insects, their writhing bodies making up his form and face, or perhaps he has a tattered human skin, with spiders occasionally crawling from one place to another on his form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T23:08:52-08:00","id":833723,"title":"","content":"Coyote is easy to swap for kitsune.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T10:44:40-07:00","id":867657,"title":"","content":"How would you change the flavor of Dearheart to match a child character who manipulates feelings of protectiveness? I've got a few ideas, but I want to crowdsource it. Thinking of calling it them Pixies, but I don't really like that name<br /> <br /> Current idea is that they are people who play the part of an adorable child (sometimes to the point you wonder what happened to their mind), though they might not even have been children when they were originally taken.<br /> <br /> Fairest looks like a beautiful, expensive doll<br /> Darkling looks like a child who has been subjected to a hard, hard life, and always seems to be in shadows<br /> Wizened looks like a worn-down, badly cared-for doll<br /> <br /> Any other ideas on stuff like different Kith Blessings?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T11:16:08-07:00","id":867678,"title":"","content":"The point of re-flavoring a Kith is to keep the mechanics, just with a different appearance. Honestly, I think Dearheart mechanics work for a &quot;manipulate others by being childlike&quot; Kith without changes.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dearhearts gain the Sympathetic Merit (p. XX). A dearheart\u2019s touch reduces the subject\u2019s Composure by half her Wyrd (rounded up), which affects any relevant traits such as Willpower, or Doors. Spend a point of Glamour while touching to learn a subject\u2019s Virtue, Vice, Needle, or Thread. Once she\u2019s done so, she may share one of her Aspirations with the target. He must share one in response or spend a Willpower point. The same Aspiration may not be shared twice. </div> </div> </div>Maybe you want to play with the looks beyond &quot;doll-like&quot;: a Beast could have large eyes, floppy ears, soft fur, and other juvenile markers; Darklings could be wrapped in a blackened blanket and always be weeping; Elementals might be a stuffed toy you can't help but want to hug; Grimms could be covered in nursery rhymes and child's drawings; Fairest could be dolls, or a star-child; Ogres could be short, chubby, and faintly green, with tiny adorable tusks poking out of their mouth; Wizened could have over-large heads and totter when they walk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T11:24:22-07:00","id":867685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/833621-kith-permutations-changing-the-flavor?p=867657#post867657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you change the flavor of Dearheart to match a child character who manipulates feelings of protectiveness? I've got a few ideas, but I want to crowdsource it. Thinking of calling it them Pixies, but I don't really like that name<br /> <br /> Current idea is that they are people who play the part of an adorable child (sometimes to the point you wonder what happened to their mind), though they might not even have been children when they were originally taken.<br /> <br /> Fairest looks like a beautiful, expensive doll<br /> Darkling looks like a child who has been subjected to a hard, hard life, and always seems to be in shadows<br /> Wizened looks like a worn-down, badly cared-for doll<br /> <br /> Any other ideas on stuff like different Kith Blessings?</div> </div> </div> </div> This childlike version of Dearheart is similar to the Playmate Kith, but the latter doesn't have the Blessing you're looking for. I would just add the Sympathetic Merit and a 1 dot or 2 dot Contract for emotional urging to the Blessing of Playmate.<br /> <br /> I'm trying to change the Grey Kith into a more general spy-themed Kith. I'll use Secret-Taker as the new name. The changelings with Grey Alien and robotic Miens would be Wizened Secret-Takers. I'd also add 2 or 3 dots in the Closed Book Merit to the Blessing of Secret-Taker, along with the original Blessing of Grey.<br /> <br /> I haven't thought of what Fairest, Darkling or Elemental Secret-Takers might look like, but here are the other Seemings:<br /> <br /> Beast: small rodents, insects and birds known for taking objects and adding them to a nest or collection, such as rats, ants and magpies.<br /> <br /> Ogre: he talks softly and has big fists. Fused to his left fist is a brass knuckle for making you talk, and to the right fist is another for making you shut up.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Ninja'd by AceOfAlmonds. The Dearheart Kith is better than Playmate. The Muse Kith is also a good option, especially as a secondary Kith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-18-2016, 02:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T11:40:59-07:00","id":867701,"title":"","content":"Playmate and Muse would work mechanics-wise, too. Dearheart's got a massive edge on direct manipulation, though, which is what the kiddie-Kith sounds like it's focused on.<br /> <br /> Secret-Taker Kith ideas:<br /> Darkling: has a suit made of shadows, and piercing, beady eyes that never stop observing (and a slight fetid reek from having to hide in fairyland's sewers more than once...)<br /> Elemental: part of a wall, with incongruous ears sticking out<br /> Fairest: tuxedo, tie, with lips that taste of martinis forming a rouge's grin. Basically James Bond, but fae-er.<br /> Grimm: covered in ciphers and symbols, interspersed with &quot;For Your Eyes Only&quot; and &quot;Top Secret&quot; and &quot;Destroy After Reading&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T12:42:13-07:00","id":867745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/833621-kith-permutations-changing-the-flavor?p=867678#post867678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point of re-flavoring a Kith is to keep the mechanics, just with a different appearance. Honestly, I think Dearheart mechanics work for a &quot;manipulate others by being childlike&quot; Kith without changes.<br /> <br /> <br /> Maybe you want to play with the looks beyond &quot;doll-like&quot;: a Beast could have large eyes, floppy ears, soft fur, and other juvenile markers; Darklings could be wrapped in a blackened blanket and always be weeping; Elementals might be a stuffed toy you can't help but want to hug; Grimms could be covered in nursery rhymes and child's drawings; Fairest could be dolls, or a star-child; Ogres could be short, chubby, and faintly green, with tiny adorable tusks poking out of their mouth; Wizened could have over-large heads and totter when they walk.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is amazing. Thank you so much. Man, I love this idea more and more<br /> <br /> EDIT: Though I don't know if sharing aspirations is something you do with kids. Maybe it's just me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T12:48:55-07:00","id":867746,"title":"","content":"Checked out the Muse kith and it sounds perfect. Not even sure I want to rename it. Now I'm gonna mess around on my own with how he'll look if I make him a Grimm or a Darkling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T13:27:07-07:00","id":867779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/833621-kith-permutations-changing-the-flavor?p=867701#post867701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Playmate and Muse would work mechanics-wise, too. Dearheart's got a massive edge on direct manipulation, though, which is what the kiddie-Kith sounds like it's focused on.<br /> <br /> Secret-Taker Kith ideas:<br /> Darkling: has a suit made of shadows, and piercing, beady eyes that never stop observing (and a slight fetid reek from having to hide in fairyland's sewers more than once...)<br /> Elemental: part of a wall, with incongruous ears sticking out<br /> Fairest: tuxedo, tie, with lips that taste of martinis forming a rouge's grin. Basically James Bond, but fae-er.<br /> Grimm: covered in ciphers and symbols, interspersed with &amp;quot;For Your Eyes Only&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;Top Secret&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;Destroy After Reading&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> Thanks for the ideas. I'd like to see a Darkling Secret-Taker + Whisperwisp + Cleareyes with Contracts of Darkness, Smoke, Mirror and Vainglory and spying Tokens competing with an experienced Unchained.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T13:36:37-07:00","id":867787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/833621-kith-permutations-changing-the-flavor?p=867779#post867779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Thanks for the ideas. I'd like to see a Darkling Secret-Taker + Whisperwisp + Cleareyes with Contracts of Darkness, Smoke, Mirror and Vainglory and spying Tokens competing with an experienced Unchained.</div> </div> </div> </div>Throw in a Mekhet and an Irraka, make it a party <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I admit some of my ideas maaaaay be more silly that serious, but I couldn't think of anything but &quot;the walls have ears&quot; for an Elemental.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T19:51:05-07:00","id":891531,"title":"","content":"A humanoid walking cloak, with limbs made of daggers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T06:02:56-07:00","id":891685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HobbitGuy1420</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/833621-kith-permutations-changing-the-flavor?p=891531#post891531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A humanoid walking cloak, with limbs made of daggers?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That basically sounds like a Elemental Razorhand","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}